s="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAMADA SHINZO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI HARUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HASHIZUME, SHUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>INOKUCHI, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, RYOUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMEI, MASANORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, SUSUMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMADA, SHINZO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUTSUMI, HARUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Drugs, foods, drinks and feeds to which a cocoa component contained in cacao mass is added to thereby achieve effects of eliminating Helicobacter pylori, promoting would healing and lowering blood ammonia level.  To add the above-described cocoa component, it is preferable to add cocoa and/or cacao mass.  In case of the foods, drinks and feeds, it is preferable to further add proteins, lipids, saccharides, vitamins and minerals as nutritional sources other than cocoa.  To achieve the effect of eliminating H. pylori, it is preferable to use the above-described cocoa component together with an antibiotic for eliminating H. pylori and/or an acid secretion inhibitor.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Dans cette invention, on ajoute à des médicaments, aliments, boissons et aliments pour animaux un composant de cacao contenu dans une pâte de cacao en vue d'éradiquer la bactérie Helicobacter pylori, favoriser la cicatrisation des plaies et réduire le taux d'ammoniac dans le sang. Afin d'ajouter le composant de cacao précité, il est préférable d'ajouter du cacao et/ou une pâte de cacao. Dans le cas d'aliments, boissons et aliments pour animaux, il est préférable d'ajouter également des protéines, des lipides, des saccharides, des vitamines et des minéraux comme sources nutritionnelles autres que le cacao. Afin d'éliminer la bactérie H. pylori, il est préférable d'utiliser le composant de cacao précité en association avec un antibiotique, de manière à éradiquer la H. pylori et/ou l'inhibiteur de sécrétion acide.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>